The root-path fix now passes the reproducer and preserves field serializers, alias configuration, explicit `by_alias`, and instance state. A parent model’s core serializer does not call a nested model’s Python `model_dump`, so the same collision remains when the affected model is serialized only as a child; fully correcting that boundary would require pydantic-core or an expensive recursive object-graph copy, both outside the mandated narrow owning-file change. I’m proceeding with the required regression suite and will audit the final diff.
